## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design scalable alerting that reduces noise while preserving critical signals, across multi-region K8s clusters, using common tools, with safe rollout.

## Key Concepts
- Alert routing and deduplication (Alertmanager, labels)
- Global blackout policy with per-region windows
- Canary rollout for rule changes; staging validation
- Metrics: alert rate, MTTA, MTTR, missed-incident risk; rollback plan

## Code Example
```javascript
// Simple in-memory alert suppression
const suppression = new Map(); // key -> timestamp until which alerts are muted
function shouldAlert(key) {
  const t = suppression.get(key);
  if (!t) return true;
  return Date.now() > t;
}
function suppress(key, durationMs) {
  suppression.set(key, Date.now() + durationMs);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you adapt this for cross-cloud regions with drift?
- How would you validate that suppression does not hide critical incidents during outages?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests practical debugging in a real-world, multi-region environment with tenant isolation. Emphasizes telemetry-driven root-cause analysis, dynamic traffic shaping, and controlled validation before rollback.

## Key Concepts

- Telemetry-driven debugging across regions
- Per-tenant isolation and rate limiting
- Cache partitioning and traffic shifting
- Progressive degradation with safe fallbacks
- Canary and synthetic test-based validation
- Rollback criteria tied to SLOs

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo: rate limiter sketch for per-tenant edge gateway
class RateLimiter {
  constructor(limitPerTenant) { this.limit = limitPerTenant; this.map = new Map(); }
  allow(tenantId) {
    const now = Date.now();
    const rec = this.map.get(tenantId) || { t: now, c: 0 };
    if (now - rec.t > 1000) { rec.t = now; rec.c = 0; }
    if (rec.c < this.limit) { rec.c++; this.map.set(tenantId, rec); return true; }
    return false;
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you measure success and determine completion of the degradation plan?
- What metrics and traces would you surface to stakeholders during the rollback decision?

## Why This Is Asked

Assess ability to design a resilient ingestion pipeline with strong delivery guarantees, backpressure handling, and multi-region failover under degraded conditions.

## Key Concepts
- Exactly-once semantics in Kafka and producers
- Idempotent processing and deduplication
- Backpressure, circuit breakers, and DLQ strategy
- Cross-region replication and failover plans
- Chaos testing for data-plane reliability

## Code Example
